msgid "Open the room in the other editor"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Open the same room in EMStudio on the desktop or on the web, or come to "
"it from EM Tools for Blender.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The graph of a room is the room's, so moving to another editor transfers "
"nothing: the other editor enters the same room and reads the same graph. "
"The link that EMStudio asks of the node carries no password or token; the"
" other editor signs itself in."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Be in the room (see :doc:`enter-and-share-a-room`). The command appears "
"only while you are in a room."
msgstr ""

msgid "Switch between the desktop and the web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the chip's menu at the top right, or click the label at the left of "
"the status bar (:kbd:`⇧⌘L` on the Mac, :kbd:`Ctrl+Shift+L` elsewhere)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the section **Where you work**, under **Room**, press **Open this room"
" in…**. EMStudio asks the node how to open the room in the other editor."
msgstr ""

msgid "Desktop"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The room opens in EMStudio for the web, the build that the node serves, "
"in the browser. If the node serves no web build of EMStudio, a message "
"says so and nothing opens."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The browser asks the system to open the desktop application on the room. "
"If no application on this computer answers, the node's page for the room "
"opens in a new tab and says what to install, and EMStudio says that "
"nothing opened."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the other editor, sign in to the node if it asks you to (see :doc"
":`sign-in`). It then enters the room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Both editors can stay in the room at the same time: each is one more "
"presence in the room, and what you change in one reaches the other as it "
"reaches every member."
msgstr ""

msgid "Come to the room from EM Tools"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EM Tools for Blender works in rooms too. When Blender is in a room, its "
"command **Open in EMStudio** opens EMStudio on the same room, with the "
"unit you chose."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If EMStudio is already in that room, it stays there and brings that unit "
"forward: nothing is signed in again."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If EMStudio is signed in on the node but in another room, or in none, it "
"enters the room with the access it already has."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Otherwise EMStudio asks you to sign in to the node first: on the desktop "
"the sign-in opens in the system's browser, on the web in the same page. "
"Then it enters the room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio has no command that opens the room in Blender: EM Tools enters "
"the room from its own panel, as its manual describes."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The same room open in the other editor, with the same graph, without a "
"copy and without a second login when a session is already there."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`enter-and-share-a-room`, on presence and roles in a room."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/reference/desktop-and-web`, for what differs between the two "
"editors."
msgstr ""

msgid ":doc:`/explanation/place-in-the-framework`, on EMStudio and EM Tools."
msgstr ""

